Apple Leaf Disease Classification Using CNN

About the Project

This project uses a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) to identify and classify different diseases in apple leaves from images. The model learns visual features from the leaf images and predicts the disease class.

Dataset

The project uses the Apple Leaf Diseases dataset from Kaggle, downloaded using KaggleHub. The dataset contains images of apple leaves belonging to different disease categories.
The images are resized to 128 × 128 pixels and divided into 80% training data and 20% validation data.

What We Do

1. Download the apple leaf disease dataset using KaggleHub.
2. Load the images and automatically detect the disease classes.
3. Resize the images to 128 × 128 pixels and normalize the pixel values.
4. Build a CNN model with three convolutional layers and max-pooling layers.
5. Train the model for 10 epochs.
6. Check training and validation accuracy and loss.
7. Generate a classification report to check the model performance for each class.
8. Create a confusion matrix to see which disease classes are correctly and incorrectly classified.

Result

The project shows how CNN can be used for image classification and automatic detection of diseases in apple leaves.

